==German==
[[File:Breads.jpg|thumb|Zwei '''Brote''' — Two '''loaves of bread''' (2)]]
[[File:Rye bread.JPG|thumb|Mehrere Scheiben Roggen'''brot''' — Several slices of rye '''bread''' (1)]]

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|de|Brod||obsolete}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|gmh|brōt}}, from {{inh|de|goh|brōt}} (attested since the 8th century), from {{inh|de|gmw-pro|*braud}}, from {{inh|de|gem-pro|*braudą}}, from {{der|de|ine-pro|*bʰrew-||to seethe, to boil}}. 

Originally, the meaning of ''Brot'' was ''"what has been fermented, leaven"'' and may be a nominal derivative from {{cog|gem-pro|*brewwaną||to brew}} (whence German {{m|de|brauen}}). It replaced the older {{m|de|Laib||loaf}} which was the more common term in Old High German (compare the use of {{m|ang|hlāf}} and {{m|ang|brēad}} in Old English).<ref>{{R:de:EWbD}}</ref>

